Azure Containers
Containers allow you to run applications without needing to deploy whole vms to reduce costs and management workloads.
They are more agile and are created to be created, configured and deleted more rapidly than vms. They are deployed as a Paas

Container types
Azure container instances - One off container instances that are used for test environments. 
Azure container apps - Serverless instances that are event-driven. 
Azure Kubernetes services - Fleet management of containers, similar to virtual machine scale sets. (Enterprise level is a key-word)

Azure functions
Event driven serverless compute option that does not allow for conatiners or vms to run. 
Used for customers who are concerned about the code running and not the underlying ifrastructure. 
Functions scale automatically based on demand. 
